From a71413e2cf243337ed04b7753787888a5dbaa2e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:48:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-rounds): read some-ui.rust-week/2 and record each
 academy starter (RR25, RR29)

paulgsc/some-ui#3249, #3257. A week may now be `some-ui.rust-week/2`: each
ticket keeps `id` and `program` as in `/1` and gains forks and an academy of
1 to 8 exercises, each with a whole `main.rs` starter. Home reads of `/2` only
what it needs (schema, id, each ticket's id and program, each academy's
starters, opens and due); the rest is kept byte for byte and never read.

- `week::read` takes `/1` and `/2`. A `/1` week reads as before (an
  `academy` on one of its tickets is not read) and keeps its 32 KiB ceiling;
  a `/2` week may be up to `WEEK_V2_CEILING` = 128 KiB, the arithmetic in its
  doc (4 tickets x 8 starters of ~1.5 KB plus prose is ~106 KB).
- Each starter is queued in `rust_round_source` after the week's ticket
  programs, in the transaction that keeps the week, and recorded by the same
  pass under the runner's unchanged 64 KiB request. No new table: programs
  are content-addressed, so a starter is one more program.
- A starter is named `<ticket>/academy/<n>` (`week::academy_key`, n from 1),
  which no ticket key can match.
- GET /rust-weeks/:id adds `academy: [{ key, ticket, exercise, sourceHash,
  runs }]` for a `/2` week; a `/1` week's answer leaves it out and is byte
  for byte as before.
- CONTRACT_EPOCH 19 -> 22 by hand for the payload change (20 and 21 are
  taken by open PRs; renumber on landing). No route changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
